  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">IANA maintains &quot;OTN Signal Type&quot; subregistry of the &quot;Generalized
Multi-Protocol Label Switching (GMPLS) Signaling Parameters&quot; registry
for OTN signal types (as defined in <xref target="RFC4328" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4328"/> and updated by
<xref target="RFC7139" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7139"/>).  This subregistry is defined to use only the Standards
Action registration policy as defined by <xref target="RFC5226" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5226"/>.  This document
updates <xref target="RFC7139" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7139"/> to allow the &quot;OTN Signal Type&quot; subregistry to also
use the Specification Required policy as defined in <xref target="RFC5226" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5226"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">This document does not introduce any new security considerations to
the existing GMPLS signaling protocols.  Refer to <xref target="RFC7139" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7139"/> for
further details of the specific security measures.  Additionally,
<xref target="RFC5920" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5920"/> provides an overview of security vulnerabilities and
protection mechanisms for the GMPLS control plane.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">IANA maintains the &quot;OTN Signal Type&quot; subregistry of the &quot;Generalized
Multi-Protocol Label Switching (GMPLS) Signaling Parameters&quot;
registry.  The registry currently is defined to use the Standards
Action registration policy as defined by <xref target="RFC5226" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5226"/>.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">Per this document, IANA has updated the registration policies for the
&quot;OTN Signal Type&quot; subregistry to be &quot;Standards Action&quot; for Standards
Track documents and &quot;Specification Required&quot; for other documents.</t>
    </section>
